## Phase 5 — Write-back

### 5a. DESIGN.md (per feature)

Location: `docs/features/<EPIC-SEQ>/DESIGN.md`.

**Path guard (non-negotiable).** Mockup HTML lands ONLY under `docs/design/<EPIC-SEQ>/screens/`. NEVER create `mockups/`, `screens/`, or `html/` under `docs/features/<EPIC-SEQ>/` — DESIGN.md lives there, so bare relative links resolve to the WRONG tree. Every screen link in DESIGN.md MUST use the `../../design/<EPIC-SEQ>/screens/<file>` form shown below. Before hand-off: verify `docs/design/<EPIC-SEQ>/screens/` is non-empty and no `.html` exists under `docs/features/<EPIC-SEQ>/`.

```markdown
# Design — <EPIC-SEQ> <Feature title>

**Provider:** html-mockup (lo-fi, no external tool)
**Bundle:** [docs/design/<EPIC-SEQ>/](../../design/<EPIC-SEQ>/)
**Generated:** <ISO8601> by ux-agent

> Lo-fi HTML mockups. Open any file under `docs/design/<EPIC-SEQ>/screens/` in a browser to view. Replace with hi-fi later by switching `integrations.design` to figma / claude-design / stitch in harness.yaml.

## Screens × form factors

| Screen | <FormFactor1> | <FormFactor2> | Components |
|---|---|---|---|
| <Screen name> | [<form1>.html](../../design/<id>/screens/<screen>-<form1>.html) | [<form2>.html](../../design/<id>/screens/<screen>-<form2>.html) | <PascalCase list from data-component attrs> |

## States covered per screen
- Populated (default, visible)
- Loading (data-state="loading", hidden by default)
- Empty (data-state="empty", hidden by default)
- Error (data-state="error", hidden by default)

## Tokens consumed
Defined in [tokens.css](../../design/<id>/tokens.css). Sourced from `docs/design/schema.json` (workspace tokens).

- Color: <list from schema.json tokens.color>
- Spacing: <list>
- Typography: <list>

## Implementation notes for /arh-implement
- Mockups are LO-FI — outline-only component placeholders with `data-component` attribute carrying the PascalCase component name
- Engineers translate `data-component="X"` to the project's real component implementation per `<framework>-patterns` Design system section
- CSS variables at `docs/design/<id>/tokens.css` map 1:1 to the project's token convention (CSS vars / Tailwind / styled-system — per <framework>-patterns)
- All four states (populated/loading/empty/error) are present in each screen; engineers must implement all four
```

