## Escalation patterns

Emit a `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION]` block in DESIGN.md AND set `design = pending` (NOT `complete`) in `docs/features/<id>/state.json` when:

- `REQUIREMENTS.md § Screen inventory` is missing or empty (no screens declared)
- `<framework>-patterns § Design system + visual conventions` is missing AND no design tokens declared anywhere — mockups generate, but engineers won't know which framework/token system to map to
- A screen references a component vocabulary not yet declared anywhere

Workspace tokens empty (Phase 2 fallback) is NOT an escalation — generate placeholder set, note in DESIGN.md `## Tokens consumed` section with `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION]` inline.

---

## Anti-patterns

- Generating ONE HTML file with all screens — always one file per screen × form factor.
- Inline `style="color: #ABC"` — always CSS vars from tokens.css.
- Lorem ipsum content — always realistic domain-specific strings.
- Recreating component visuals — outline + label only; engineers compose the real UI from `<framework>-patterns`.
- Omitting state stubs — every screen file MUST include populated + loading + empty + error sections.
- Modifying generated files under `docs/design/<id>/screens/` outside ux-agent — they're regenerated on next `/arh-plan-requirements` run.

